 61NI    60NI(A,3HE)                   2013SC06,2013SCZZ         ENSDF    202006
 61NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=20-Jan-2020$                    
 61NI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=KAZIMIERZ ZUBER, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 125, 1 (2015)$       
 61NI2 H CUT=25-Jan-2015$                                                       
 61NI c  No changes made since the 2015 update                                  
 61NI c  2013Sc06, 2013ScZZ: E(|a)=38 MeV from WNSL-Yale tandem                 
 61NI2c  accelerator facility. Measured {+3}He spectra, |s(|q), spectroscopic   
 61NI3c  factors C{+2}S using a split-pole Enge spectrograph. FWHM |?50 keV.    
 61NI4c  Target=204 |mg/cm{+2} thick 99.7% enriched. Deduced levels, J, |p.     
 61NI5c  DWBA analysis. Comparison with shell-model calculations.               
 61NI c  The main purpose of the neutron adding and neutron removal reaction    
 61NI2c  studies by 2013Sc06 was to obtain occupancies of neutron orbitals,     
 61NI3c  proton vacancies, and energy centroids of neutron, neutron-holes,      
 61NI4c  proton-single particle excitations in {+60}Ni and {+62}Ni, and thereby 
 61NI5c  investigate closure of 0f{-7/2} shell. Some data details of this study 
 61NI6c  are supplied in 2013ScZZ                                               
 61NI c  Other:                                                                 
 61NI c  1961Sa09: E=43 MeV. Measured E({+3}He), magnetic spectrometer,         
 61NI2c  |q=22|'. Three groups at 0, 1700 and 2700 are reported; the 1700- and  
 61NI3c  and 2700-keV peaks cannot be easily assigned to those observed in      
 61NI4c  spectral figure 2 in 2013Sc06. There are either calibration issues     
 61NI5c  or contribution from impurities                                        
 61NI c  The uncertainties in d|s/d|W are estimated to be |?4% for |s>1 mb/sr,  
 61NI2c  |?7% for 0.1<|s< 1.0 mb/sr, and |?18% for |s< 0.1 mb/sr at their       
 61NI3c  respective maxima. The uncertainties arising from possible contaminants
 61NI4c  or previously unidentified states for very weak transitions could be   
 61NI5c  |?0.02 mb/sr.                                                          
